  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "One BOUNDARY per service pair",
      "items": [
        "(:Service)-[:BOUNDARY {via, evidence}]->(:Service), consumer to provider",
        "via lists every kind of evidence found; evidence lists the underlying edges",
        "Computed after all other link edges, from the graph alone"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Adding a new cross-service link (e.g. gRPC)",
      "items": [
        "1. Parser: record the fact on the Symbol (e.g. grpc_calls {service, method, line}), Task 4",
        "2. Store it as a node property so link never re-parses, Task 6",
        "3. graph::link: resolve it to an edge (e.g. CALLS_RPC) and add the rel to LINK_RELS",
        "4. BOUNDARY rule: add the new via value; 5. fixture + test, then teach trace_flow to follow it"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Why links live in one place",
      "items": [
        "Incremental indexing deletes and recomputes every LINK_RELS edge each run",
        "So a change in one service updates its boundaries with others automatically",
        "Name-based resolution is a marked ponytail; LSP can sharpen it later"
      ]
    }
  ]
